    {
      "id": "vl42Juvp7UQpvNAgmTFG6",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1960.5516031509023,
      "y": -472.1583800565172,
      "width": 745.95947265625,
      "height": 925,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "qXKs2yDD1YNlc1XTBri7N",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1745643312,
      "version": 1090,
      "versionNonce": 1515719667,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783837014055,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Neetcode\n1. Sorting\n- .sort vs sorted(), .sort() preferred since in-line and more memory optimized\n- awareness of keywords and params to leverage default native language \n\n2. pythonic programming \n- unpacking\n- enumerate1 \n- zip\n- inequiality\n- min(), max()\n\n3. lists\n4. Stacks & Queues\n5. 2D lists\n6. Hashmap and Hashsets\n7. Heaps/Priority Queues\n8. Sorted Dicts and Sorted Sets\n\n--\n\nNeetcode cont.\n\nTree traversal vs. Linked-list traversal\nclass TreeNode:\n    def __init__(self, val=0, left=None, right=None):\n        self.val = val\n        self.left = left\n        self.right = right\n\n--\nStandard Libraries to know\n1. collections\n2. heapq\n3. bisect\n4. defaultdict\n    - convienent way to initiate values of dicts",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Neetcode\n1. Sorting\n- .sort vs sorted(), .sort() preferred since in-line and more memory optimized\n- awareness of keywords and params to leverage default native language \n\n2. pythonic programming \n- unpacking\n- enumerate1 \n- zip\n- inequiality\n- min(), max()\n\n3. lists\n4. Stacks & Queues\n5. 2D lists\n6. Hashmap and Hashsets\n7. Heaps/Priority Queues\n8. Sorted Dicts and Sorted Sets\n\n--\n\nNeetcode cont.\n\nTree traversal vs. Linked-list traversal\nclass TreeNode:\n    def __init__(self, val=0, left=None, right=None):\n        self.val = val\n        self.left = left\n        self.right = right\n\n--\nStandard Libraries to know\n1. collections\n2. heapq\n3. bisect\n4. defaultdict\n    - convienent way to initiate values of dicts",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "rW93iFSDYkqgwgt0Ju_-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -986.3250976811105,
      "y": -473.84609882697555,
      "width": 933.9393310546875,
      "height": 875,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "qXKs2yDD1YNlc1XTBri7N",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1045942224,
      "version": 1100,
      "versionNonce": 1576539539,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783837014055,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Learning Python (book)\n1. FUNDAMENTALS\n- numbers & expressions\n- dynamic typing\n- strings\n    - print f\"string{var}\"\n- lists and dictionary\n    - list.append vs. list.extend\n- tuples1\n\n2. LOGICAL FLOW\n- if/else\n- for, while loops\n- comprehensions\n- pass, continue, break\n\n3. FUNCTIONS\n- functions (def my_func(args: args_type = default_value) -> return.type:\n- lambda single_arg:\n\n4. MODULES\n- import ...\n- from ... import ...\n- Could be our own scripts\n    - requires __init__.py at top of folder structure\n\n5. CLASSES & OBJECT ORIENTATED PROGRAMMING\nClass MyClass:\n    def __init__(self, my_param: param.type) -> None:\n        self.my_param = my_param # self creates an instance of the varaible for use downstream\n\n    def my_method(self) -> None:\n\n6. EXCEPTIONS & TESTING1\n        ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Learning Python (book)\n1. FUNDAMENTALS\n- numbers & expressions\n- dynamic typing\n- strings\n    - print f\"string{var}\"\n- lists and dictionary\n    - list.append vs. list.extend\n- tuples1\n\n2. LOGICAL FLOW\n- if/else\n- for, while loops\n- comprehensions\n- pass, continue, break\n\n3. FUNCTIONS\n- functions (def my_func(args: args_type = default_value) -> return.type:\n- lambda single_arg:\n\n4. MODULES\n- import ...\n- from ... import ...\n- Could be our own scripts\n    - requires __init__.py at top of folder structure\n\n5. CLASSES & OBJECT ORIENTATED PROGRAMMING\nClass MyClass:\n    def __init__(self, my_param: param.type) -> None:\n        self.my_param = my_param # self creates an instance of the varaible for use downstream\n\n    def my_method(self) -> None:\n\n6. EXCEPTIONS & TESTING1\n        ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
